API-07: count check-valve pipes as pipes when deleting a link

EN_deletelink decremented Npipes only for links of type PIPE. A pipe
with a check valve has type CVPIPE (0), which EN_addlink and the input
parser count as a pipe (linkType <= PIPE), so each deleted check-valve
pipe left the count one too high. The fix for #790 (commit d50c673)
added the decrement; this extends it to CVPIPE.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-07_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..872ece2 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -3599,8 +3599,9 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_deletelink(EN_Project p, int index, int actionCode)
         if (net->Valve[i].Link > index) net->Valve[i].Link -= 1;
     }
 
-    // Reduce the number of pipes count by one if it is a pipe.
-    if (linkType == PIPE)
+    // Reduce the number of pipes count by one if it is a pipe
+    // (with or without a check valve).
+    if (linkType <= PIPE)
     {
         net->Npipes--;
     }
